List the Go toolchains and Go tools available in go-overlay, without
cloning the repository or compiling anything.

By default, shows the newest release of each minor version. A PREFIX lists
every release whose version starts with it, so 1.24 lists every 1.24 release
and 1.2 widens to 1.20 through 1.29. Each row's PACKAGE is a flake output
that can be used directly, for example:

  nix shell github:purpleclay/go-overlay#go_1_25_5

Name a TOOL to list its versions instead. Its PACKAGE is the attribute to
use from a toolchain, which can also be used directly:

  nix shell 'github:purpleclay/go-overlay#go.tools.gopls."0.24.0"'

USAGE

  goversions [FLAGS] [PREFIX]
  goversions [FLAGS] TOOL [PREFIX]
  goversions --tools [--go VERSION]

EXAMPLES

  # List the newest release of each minor version
  goversions

  # List every 1.24 release
  goversions 1.24

  # List every release
  goversions --all

  # List every 1.24 release as a JSON array
  goversions --json 1.24

  # List every tool and its latest version
  goversions --tools

  # List the newest gopls release of each minor version
  goversions gopls

  # List the gopls versions that work with Go 1.26
  goversions gopls --go 1.26

FLAGS

  -a, --all
          list every version, not just the newest per minor

  -g, --go VERSION
          only list tool versions that work with this Go version

  -h, --help
          help for goversions

  -j, --json
          print every matching version as a JSON array

  -t, --tools
          list every tool and its latest version

  -V, --version
          print the goversions version

STATUSES

  latest      the newest release; latest (stable) when it is also the newest
              stable release
  stable      the newest stable release, shown when an rc is newer
  supported   a stable release in a release line Go still supports
  prerelease  an rc or beta in a release line Go still supports
  eol         any release in a release line Go no longer supports

EXIT CODES

  0  versions listed
  1  no versions match PREFIX or --go
  2  bad flags or arguments
